 {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "1385 reaches 1186 only via 3-hop untimed routes through the hubs 528 (72 in-neighbours) or 1818 (26 in-neighbours). Both endpoints fire each edge essentially once (11 and 9 events over 11 and 9 partners), so each candidate chain has a single timing realisation, and the 600-unit relay budget covers only ~1.6% of the 38k-wide query window. The connectivity is therefore attributable to hub popularity and time-ignored reachability rather than a genuine time-respecting cascade; no delay-constrained chain is supported."}, "raw_final_response": "## Analysis\n\n**Static reachability (necessary but not sufficient):** 1385 has 7 out-neighbours {379, 457, 595, 639, 675, 1409, 1688} (step_03); 1186 has only 3 in-neighbours {528, 1259, 1818} (step_04). Intersecting: 528's in-set contains 595, 639, 1688 (step_06) and 1818's in-set contains 639 (step_08); 1259's in-set is disjoint (step_07). So the *only* untimed routes are 3-hop chains 1385\u2192{595,639,1688}\u2192528\u21921186 and 1385\u2192639\u21921818\u21921186.\n\n**Why that is not enough:**\n- Both endpoints are extremely sparse: 1385 has 11 events over 11 distinct partners, 1186 has 9 events over 9 partners (step_02) \u2014 essentially every edge fires once, so each candidate chain has exactly one timing realisation, with no repeat attempts to \"get lucky\".\n- The junction node 528 is a hub with 72 distinct in-neighbours (step_06), and 1818 has 26 (step_08). Their appearance on the path is explained by generic popularity, not by a targeted relay \u2014 a classic confounder for cascade claims.\n- The graph has 16,325 events over 15,458 distinct edges (repeat ratio 0.053, step_01) spread across a horizon of ~100,000; the queried window is ~38,400 units wide while the allowed relay gap is only 600 units (\u22481.6 % of the window). For a single-realisation 3-hop chain, two consecutive gaps both landing under 600 units is a low-probability event, and nothing in the observed structure indicates it occurred.\n\nNo temporal chain from 1385 to 1186 with per-hop delay \u2264 600 is supported; the connection that exists is a time-ignored, hub-mediated one.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_8980b60f\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1385, 1186, 528, 1818, 595, 639, 1688],\n  \"window\": [61549, 99948],\n  \"confidence\": 0.62,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"1385 reaches 1186 only via 3-hop untimed routes through the hubs 528 (72 in-neighbours) or 1818 (26 in-neighbours). Both endpoints fire each edge essentially once (11 and 9 events over 11 and 9 partners), so each candidate chain has a single timing realisation, and the 600-unit relay budget covers only ~1.6% of the 38k-wide query window. The connectivity is therefore attributable to hub popularity and time-ignored reachability rather than a genuine time-respecting cascade; no delay-constrained chain is supported.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 14292, "total_output_tokens": 2651, "total_tokens": 16943, "total_latency_ms": 37815, "llm_calls": 4, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}